course: dictionary
lesson: 7177
title: One word, four meanings: Persian
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names of places or peoples, and they can change meaning depending on the words next to them. «Together they faced the mighty Persian Empire at Marathon and Thermopylae.» Here Persian describes the empire. It tells you where the empire came from: Persia, the old name for Iran.
explain: The same word can name a person, a language or an animal. Look at the word after Persian. In «Persian Empire» and «Persian carpet», Persian describes a thing. In «a Persian cat», it names a breed. In «Persian is spoken in Iran», it names the language. The clue is always in the words around it.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The Persian Gulf» is the sea between Iran and Arabia, so you can swap in "the sea between Iran and Arabia" and it still makes sense. If your swap does not fit, look again at the clues.
fact: Persian describes Persia, the old name for Iran, and its people, history and culture.
fact: Persian, also called Farsi, is the main language of Iran, and it is also spoken in Afghanistan and Tajikistan.
fact: A Persian is a person from Persia or Iran, and a Persian cat has long fluffy fur and a flat face.
fact: A Persian carpet is a hand-woven carpet with rich patterns.
fact: «The Persian Gulf» is the sea between Iran and Arabia.
exercise: «Together they faced the mighty Persian Empire at Marathon and Thermopylae.» What does Persian describe here? | A sea between two lands | A type of cat with long fluffy fur | A language spoken in classrooms | *A great empire from Persia, the old name for Iran
exercise: Nadia says Farsi is another name for which language? | *Persian | Hindi | Arabic | Russian
exercise: Grandma's living room has a Persian carpet with rich patterns. What is a Persian carpet? | A flat stone on a garden path | A kind of cat | A carpet made from plastic | *A carpet woven by hand, with rich patterns
test: «The Persian Gulf lies between Iran and Arabia.» What is the Persian Gulf? | *A sea between Iran and Arabia | A city in Afghanistan | A river in Tajikistan | A mountain range in Iran
test: Dad says, «Our new Persian has long fluffy fur and a flat face.» What is a Persian here? | A person from Persia | A hand-woven rug | *A cat breed with long fluffy fur | A language spoken in Iran
exam: In which sentence does Persian mean a person from Iran? | The Persian language is taught in the school | The Persian carpet was very old and soft | The Persian cat slept on the sofa all day | *Ali is a Persian who came to London from Iran
